# Scope

Production portable_prelaunch_menu and renderer ran in a new owned Win32 console.
HOME, USERPROFILE, APPDATA, LOCALAPPDATA, config, workspace and temporary paths were
fresh private fixture directories. Runtime/provider/credential environment was
scrubbed; only an owned loopback model catalogue fixture was contacted. No real
Claude session, provider, personal settings file, draft queue or feedback send was
used. Parent source files were read, not changed by this verification.

# Observed

- The fixture config omitted claude_feedback_drafts. The production menu rendered
  Claude feedback drafts [off (default)].
- Real Enter key events changed the row to [on], then [off (default)]. Each step
  was read back from the temporary config.json as a root boolean.
- Each choice was independently loaded through production ciel_runtime.env_vars,
  applied after production projected-key cleanup, and sent to a new real owned
  Python child. The child observed CLAUDE_CODE_SEND_FEEDBACK=0, 1, 0 respectively.
- The probe parent deliberately carried CLAUDE_CODE_SEND_FEEDBACK=1; default-off
  and explicit-off both replaced it with 0.
- The menu exited with code 0. Owned menu process exited and fixture listener was
  closed. result.json records all assertions, environment observations, source
  hashes and pixel-capture outcomes.

# Evidence

- 01-main.txt: actual production main menu console buffer.
- 02-feedback-default-off.txt: selected feedback row, default off.
- 03-feedback-on.txt: real key toggle on and next-launch explanatory message.
- 04-feedback-off.txt: real key toggle off and next-launch explanatory message.
- child-environment-probes.json: real child process environment 0 -> 1 -> 0.
- result.json: final passed status, menu exit code 0 and closed owned resources.
- capture_menu.py, menu_bootstrap.py, projection_probe.py, console_driver.py:
  exact reproduction harness and Win32 console input/output driver.

# Limits

PrintWindow was attempted only against the owned console handle. All four
attempts reported window not found; no PNG was produced. The .txt files are
ReadConsoleOutputCharacterW captures, not pixel screenshots or synthetic UI.
No actual Claude feedback draft was triggered or sent. This verifies menu
persistence and new-child launch environment, not remote account eligibility.
